# Rust normalization is a DEGRADED tier by design (DEC-012), and this case
# pins both halves of that bargain.
#
# What it catches: `Beta::accumulate` is `Alpha::total` reformatted,
# re-commented, and renamed. Layout and comments never reach the hash because
# only leaf tokens are folded, and a function's own name is excluded exactly
# as in Ruby — so the two collide.
#
# What it does NOT catch: `Gamma::total` is the same computation with renamed
# locals and parameters. Ruby's normalization sees through a rename; the token
# stream cannot, so Gamma stands alone. Recorded deliberately — if Rust ever
# gains real normalization this line is the first thing that should change,
# and until then nobody should believe the tiers are equivalent.
#
# `Delta::total` subtracts where the others add: a real difference, and the
# control that proves the collisions above are not everything colliding.
dupes  app::Alpha::total+app::Beta::accumulate
